WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.391 --> 00:00:15.512
By the time Nina got to Kids Central, everyone was already hula hooping.

2
00:00:19.633 --> 00:00:21.493
we having another hula hoop day?"

3
00:00:21.893 --> 00:00:23.474
Nina asked excitedly.

4
00:00:23.494 --> 00:00:25.294
"Where's Izzie?"

5
00:00:25.314 --> 00:00:28.195
"Izzie wasn't feeling well.

6
00:00:29.215 --> 00:00:32.761
So she stayed home from school today," Miss Shelly told Nina.

7
00:00:32.781 --> 00:00:37.284
"And we are using hula hoops again, but in a different way."

8
00:00:38.745 --> 00:00:42.328
Nina took off her backpack and sat down between Bobby and Ethan.

9
00:00:44.249 --> 00:00:47.171
She smiled at Jason, who was sitting across from her.

10
00:00:47.191 --> 00:00:50.534
"It's almost holiday season.

11
00:00:51.354 --> 00:00:53.476
Did any of you decorate your houses yet?"

12
00:00:53.816 --> 00:00:54.837
Miss Shelly asked.

13
00:00:55.717 --> 00:00:59.100
"We put Christmas lights in our front yard," Nina said.

14
00:01:00.408 --> 00:01:03.429
"We put candles in our menorah," Jason said.

15
00:01:03.449 --> 00:01:06.070
"We put up a Christmas tree with lights!"

16
00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:07.330
Ethan said.

17
00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:12.191
"Aren't lights and candles a pretty way to spread holiday spirit?

18
00:01:13.191 --> 00:01:17.333
My favorite decoration is a wreath of lights," Miss Shelly said.

19
00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:22.834
She showed them a photo of a bright, white wreath.

20
00:01:23.854 --> 00:01:24.915
It was made of lights!

21
00:01:24.935 --> 00:01:31.181
"Oh! I wish we had a wreath like that in here," Nina whispered.

22
00:01:31.201 --> 00:01:36.264
"We will have a wreath like that after today," Miss Shelly said.

23
00:01:39.426 --> 00:01:43.009
Miss Shelly rolled out the biggest hula hoop Nina had ever seen.

24
00:01:49.594 --> 00:01:51.635
Too bad Izzie isn't here to see this!"

25
00:01:52.195 --> 00:01:52.816
Nina said.

26
00:01:52.836 --> 00:01:55.618
"Is that going to be our wreath?"

27
00:01:56.078 --> 00:01:56.879
Bobby asked.

28
00:01:58.139 --> 00:02:02.229
"Yes! We'll wrap lights around it," Miss Shelly said.

29
00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:08.130
Miss Shelly opened a box and pulled out a string of lights.

30
00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:11.191
"Tape one end to the hula hoop.

31
00:02:12.952 --> 00:02:15.192
Wrap the rest of the string around the hoop.

32
00:02:18.313 --> 00:02:21.974
When you're done, connect it to another string and keep going!"

33
00:02:23.114 --> 00:02:25.695
Everyone worked hard wrapping lights around the hoop.

34
00:02:26.835 --> 00:02:29.116
Finally the boxes of lights were empty.

35
00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:36.082
"I can't even see the hula hoop anymore!"

36
00:02:36.543 --> 00:02:37.203
Nina said.

37
00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:41.087
"Let's plug in our wreath," Miss Shelly said.

38
00:02:46.571 --> 00:02:48.133
The kids all cried together.

39
00:02:48.153 --> 00:02:52.076
"I bet you can see it from outer space!"

40
00:02:52.497 --> 00:02:53.237
Bobby said.

41
00:02:53.257 --> 00:02:57.621
"Why are the lights out in here?"

42
00:02:58.682 --> 00:03:00.564
Ms. Folani stuck her head in the door.

43
00:03:03.496 --> 00:03:04.617
"Is everything okay?"

44
00:03:06.078 --> 00:03:06.518
Then Ms.

45
00:03:06.538 --> 00:03:07.859
Folani noticed the wreath.

46
00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:10.221
"That's beautiful!

47
00:03:10.321 --> 00:03:12.043
Is this the work of Kids Central?"

48
00:03:12.463 --> 00:03:14.144
she asked.

49
00:03:14.164 --> 00:03:17.107
"Yep." Nina nodded proudly.

50
00:03:18.247 --> 00:03:19.789
Miss Shelly looked proud too.

51
00:03:19.809 --> 00:03:23.351
"I know a great spot for that wreath!"

52
00:03:23.812 --> 00:03:24.852
Ms. Folani said.

53
00:03:24.872 --> 00:03:27.294
"On the front of our school!

54
00:03:28.455 --> 00:03:29.276
What do you think?"

55
00:03:30.252 --> 00:03:33.575
The principal looked at Nina, Bobby, Ethan, and Jason.

56
00:03:34.656 --> 00:03:35.556
Ethan grinned.

57
00:03:35.576 --> 00:03:38.139
"I think it's a great idea!"

58
00:03:38.159 --> 00:03:41.281
"So do I," Jason agreed.

59
00:03:41.301 --> 00:03:44.684
"Hey, aren't you missing somebody?"

60
00:03:45.104 --> 00:03:46.265
Ms. Folani asked.

61
00:03:47.286 --> 00:03:50.008
"Izzie stayed home sick today," Nina said.

62
00:03:50.028 --> 00:03:53.531
"But I bet she would say it's a good idea too."

63
00:03:56.814 --> 00:03:59.236
The kids carried the wreath out the front door.

64
00:04:01.684 --> 00:04:02.906
Miss Shelly plugged it in.

65
00:04:03.867 --> 00:04:07.251
The warm glow of the lights reflected off the snowy ground.

66
00:04:08.352 --> 00:04:11.156
Nina couldn't wait to show the wreath to Izzie tomorrow.
